    <description>Called by Opportunity - Closed Won - After Save with the Opportunity Id. Finds the Opportunity&apos;s Approved Quote and stops if there isn&apos;t one. Creates the Contract with the native Create Contract action (net unit prices saved as contract prices), sets its Contract Term from the quote lines if blank (Create Contract leaves it blank, so the Contract would have no End Date) and activates it. Creates the Order with the native Create Orders From Quote action and activates it, which fires Order - Create Assets. Then checks Closed Won Automation Complete, clears Closed Won Automation Error, links the Contract to the Opportunity and copies the Contract&apos;s Start Date and End Date to License Start Date and License End Date. Re-uses a Contract or Order that already exists for the Quote, and does nothing if the automation has already completed, so re-running it doesn&apos;t create duplicates. Any error is written to Closed Won Automation Error and sent through the Fault Path Subflow. The renewal Opportunity and Quote are created later by Order - Assets Created - Create Renewal, once the Assets exist.</description>
    <environments>Default</environments>
    <formulas>
        <description>Contract Term in months, from the Contract Start Date to the day after the latest quote line End Date (e.g. 2 Nov 2026 to 1 Nov 2027 = 12).</description>
        <name>formContractTerm</name>
        <dataType>Number</dataType>
        <expression>( YEAR( {!Get_Latest_Quote_Line.EndDate} + 1 ) - YEAR( {!Get_Contract.StartDate} ) ) * 12 + MONTH( {!Get_Latest_Quote_Line.EndDate} + 1 ) - MONTH( {!Get_Contract.StartDate} )</expression>
        <scale>0</scale>
    </formulas>
    <interviewLabel>Closed Won Revenue Automation {!$Flow.CurrentDateTime}</interviewLabel>
    <label>Closed Won Revenue Automation</label>
    <processMetadataValues>
        <name>BuilderType</name>
        <value>
            <stringValue>LightningFlowBuilder</stringValue>
        </value>
